module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ReesChartFraction
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ReesChartIdealTransport
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ReesPieceCentre
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersionFinitePresentation.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.AwayKernel
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ChartKernel
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.FiniteTypePresentationOffSupport

/-!
# The second centre of a blowup

Let `X` be a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme, let `I` be a finite-type quasi-coherent ideal
sheaf on it, let `b : Bl_I(X) ⟶ X` be the blowup and `E` its exceptional ideal sheaf. Given a
second finite-type centre `Z` on `Bl_I(X)`, [Stacks, Tag 080B] produces a `d > 0` and a
finite-type centre `J ≤ I ^ d` on `X` itself whose inverse image on the blowup factors as
`b⁻¹J · 𝒪 = E ^ d · Z`. This file proves that existence statement.

The proof is Stacks Lemma 31.32.5 — [Stacks, Tag 0803] — applied to the Rees algebra `⨁ Iⁿ`:
`Z` is transported to a closed subscheme of the relative `Proj` of that algebra, Tag 0803
presents the subscheme as the relative `Proj` of a quotient by the graded ideal generated by a
quasi-coherent finite-type submodule `ℱ` of one homogeneous piece `(⨁ Iⁿ)_d`, and `ℱ` read as a
centre on `X` is the `J` wanted.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_secondCentre`: **[Stacks, Tag 080B]** — the second centre exists.

## Implementation notes

Both halves of the statement about `J` are already theorems about
`Stacks.Blowup.reesCentre I ℱ`, the centre attached to `ℱ` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ReesPieceCentre.lean`: its containment in `I ^ d` is
`Stacks.Blowup.reesCentre_le_pow` and its finite type is
`Stacks.Blowup.isFiniteType_reesCentre`. At that centre the chart criterion of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/CentreNormalizeChart.lean` reads as
`Stacks.Blowup.comap_reesCentre_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff`, which reduces the
factorization to one statement per standard affine chart `Γ(X, U)[I/a]` of the blowup: that `Z`
is generated there by the fractions `x / aᵈ` for `x` a local section of `ℱ` over `U`. All the
work of this file is the proof of that statement, `map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq_span`, and it is a
chain of four identifications of one and the same ideal.

* `Stacks.Blowup.map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq_map_chartAwayEquiv` moves `Z`'s ideal from the standard
  blowup chart to the degree-one `Proj` chart `D₊(a)` of the Rees algebra on the
  `SheafGradedAlgebra` substrate, along `Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayEquiv`.
* `comap_awayChart_eq` identifies the inverse image of `Z` on that chart with the kernel ideal
  sheaf of `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` applied to the graded quotient of the presentation. The
  chart of `Stacks.Blowup.awayChart` is a composite of three morphisms by definition, so this is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp` twice, `ker_subschemeι` and the `iso_comp`
  clause of the presentation to replace the closed immersion by
  `…ProjBundleSurjection.map`, and the chart square
  `…ProjBundleSurjection.isPullback_chart` to restrict that kernel to the chart.
* `Stacks.ProjAwayKernel.map_ΓSpecIso_ideal_comap_awayι` reads that kernel ideal sheaf on the
  chart as the ring-theoretic kernel of `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map`.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ker_awayMap_sectionHom_eq_span_degreeOne` computes that kernel, the
  denominator being of degree one, as the span of the single fractions `s / aᵈ` with `s` a local
  section of `ℱ`.

What is left is to recognise each of those fractions, pushed through `chartAwayEquiv`, as the
affine blowup algebra's `affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction`: that is
`chartAwayEquiv_awayMk_of`, which routes the fraction through
`AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation` by `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map_mk` and lands it with
`Stacks.Blowup.reesToAffineBlowupEquiv_awayMk` and
`Stacks.Blowup.reesToBase_reesChartGradedHom_of`. The two index types of the two spans —
`Γ(ℱ.toSheafOfModules, U)` and `↥(ℱ.toSubmodule.obj (op U))` — are the same type, and
`reesPieceAmbient_eq_structureAppₗ` records that the image of a local section of `ℱ` in
`Γ(X, U)` is the one `Stacks.Blowup.reesPieceAmbient` gives it, so the two generating families
agree on the nose.

The proofs here are written in term mode, through `Eq.trans` and `congrArg` with explicitly
ascribed lambdas, rather than by `rw`: rewriting abstracts a motive over an ideal sheaf of the
relative `Proj` of the Rees algebra, or over a morphism out of it, and type-checking that motive
exhausts the heartbeat budget. For the same reason `comap_congr` is stated once, for abstract
schemes. One spelling matters: the `GradedRing` instance on a graded ring of sections must be
written as `(𝒜.toGradedAlgebra).grading U` rather than `𝒜.grading U.toOpens` inside the
statement of `awayMk_reesChartGradedInv_hom`, since
`…RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.grading` is an `abbrev` and the instance for the reduced
spelling is not found there.

## Not done here

Only the factorization is proved. The support statement of [Stacks, Tag 080B] — that `J` may be
chosen with `Supp J ⊆ Supp I ∪ b(Supp Z)` — is not: Tag 0803 is applied with the empty open, so
its conclusion about the support of the cokernel of `ℱ` is discarded. The support identity does
follow from the factorization alone, by `AlgebraicGeometry.supportSet_mul_eq_union_image` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/CompositeCentre.lean`, but is not restated here.
Nothing is said about the uniqueness of `d` or of `J`, and
the consequence for admissible blowups, [Stacks, Tag 080L], is
`Stacks.Blowup.IsAdmissibleBlowup.comp_of_secondCentreIdeal` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/AdmissibleComposition.lean`, which is not discharged here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 080B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0803](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0803)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPresentation
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartBaseChange (awayMk_congr)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The kernel ideal sheaf of a base change of a closed immersion is the inverse image of the
kernel ideal sheaf of that closed immersion.

This restates `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_eq_comap_ker_of_isPullback` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Chow/UniversalPrincipalDivisor/ZeroIdeal.lean`, whose file is not
imported here: it belongs to the Chow tree, which this file has no other reason to depend on. -/
private theorem ker_eq_comap_ker_of_isPullback' {W Y Z T : Scheme.{u}}
    {p : W ⟶ Y} {q : W ⟶ Z} {f : Y ⟶ T} {j : Z ⟶ T} [IsClosedImmersion j]
    (h : IsPullback p q f j) : p.ker = j.ker.comap f := by
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_fst_of_isClosedImmersion j f, ← h.isoPullback_hom_fst,
    Scheme.Hom.ker_comp_of_isIso]

/-- Two equal ideal sheaves have equal inverse images. Stated with the morphism first and as a
plain `congrArg` behind an explicitly ascribed lambda, so that applying it never abstracts a
motive over the relative `Proj` of the Rees algebra. -/
private theorem comap_congr {Y T : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ T) {K L : T.IdealSheafData} (h : K = L) :
    K.comap f = L.comap f :=
  congrArg (fun M : T.IdealSheafData => M.comap f) h

/-- Equal morphisms have equal kernel ideal sheaves, stated like `comap_congr`. -/
private theorem ker_congr {Y T : Scheme.{u}} {f g : Y ⟶ T} (h : f = g) : f.ker = g.ker :=
  congrArg (fun k : Y ⟶ T => k.ker) h

section Chart

variable (I : X.IdealSheafData) {d : ℕ}
  (ℱ : ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).piece (d : ℤ)).Submodule)
  (Z : (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I).IdealSheafData)
  (pres : DegreeQuotientPresentation (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I)
    (Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom).subschemeι ℱ)
  (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U)

/-- The graded quotient map of the presentation, read on the chart over `U`. -/
private abbrev presChartMap :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (pres.target.grading (chartSite U).toOpens) ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).grading (chartSite U).toOpens) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map (pres.hom.sectionHom (chartSite U).toOpens)
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.irrelevant_le_map_sectionHom
      pres.surjective (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U)))

/-- The chart map of the presentation is a closed immersion. -/
private theorem isClosedImmersion_presChartMap :
    IsClosedImmersion (presChartMap I ℱ Z pres U) := by
  have h := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.isClosedImmersion_chartMap
    pres.surjective (chartSite U).toOpens (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))
  rwa [Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.chartMap_eq_map] at h

/-- The ideal sheaf cut out by the presentation on the `Proj` chart over `U` is the kernel of the
chart map of the presentation. -/
private theorem comap_chart_eq_ker_presChartMap :
    (Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom).comap
        ((relativeProj (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I)).chart (chartSite U).toOpens
          (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))) = (presChartMap I ℱ Z pres U).ker := by
  have := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.isClosedImmersion_map pres.surjective
  have h1 : Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom =
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.map pres.surjective).ker :=
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι (Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom)).symm.trans
      ((ker_congr pres.iso_comp).symm.trans (Scheme.Hom.ker_comp_of_isIso pres.iso.hom _))
  have h2 : (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.chartMap pres.surjective
        (chartSite U).toOpens (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))).ker =
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.map pres.surjective).ker.comap
        ((relativeProj (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I)).chart (chartSite U).toOpens
          (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))) :=
    ker_eq_comap_ker_of_isPullback'
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.isPullback_chart pres.surjective
        (chartSite U).toOpens (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))).flip
  refine Eq.trans (comap_congr _ h1) ?_
  exact h2.symm.trans (ker_congr
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.chartMap_eq_map pres.surjective
      (chartSite U).toOpens (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))))

/-- The transported second centre, read on the degree-one `Proj` chart at `a`, is the kernel of
the chart map of the presentation. -/
private theorem comap_awayChart_eq :
    Z.comap (awayChart I U a) =
      (presChartMap I ℱ Z pres U).ker.comap
        (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι
          (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
          (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a) (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a) Nat.one_pos) := by
  have h0 : Z.comap (awayChart I U a) =
      ((Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom).comap
          ((relativeProj (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I)).chart (chartSite U).toOpens
            (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U)))).comap
        (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι
          (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
          (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a) (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a) Nat.one_pos) :=
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp Z _ _).trans
      (comap_congr _ (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp Z _ _))
  exact h0.trans (comap_congr _ (comap_chart_eq_ker_presChartMap I ℱ Z pres U))

/-- The transported second centre, read as an ideal of the degree-one `Proj` chart's coordinate
ring, is the kernel of the induced map of away-localizations. -/
private theorem map_ΓSpecIso_ideal_comap_awayChart :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (HomogeneousLocalization.Away
          (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
          (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a)))).hom.hom
        ((Z.comap (awayChart I U a)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top_chartAway I U a⟩) =
      RingHom.ker (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map
        (pres.hom.sectionHom (chartSite U).toOpens) (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a)) := by
  have := isClosedImmersion_presChartMap I ℱ Z pres U
  have : QuasiCompact (presChartMap I ℱ Z pres U) := inferInstance
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun K : (Spec (.of (HomogeneousLocalization.Away
        (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
        (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a)))).IdealSheafData =>
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (HomogeneousLocalization.Away
          (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
          (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a)))).hom.hom
        (K.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top_chartAway I U a⟩))
    (comap_awayChart_eq I ℱ Z pres U a)) ?_
  exact Stacks.ProjAwayKernel.map_ΓSpecIso_ideal_comap_awayι
    (pres.hom.sectionHom (chartSite U).toOpens) _ (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a) Nat.one_pos

/-- The two spellings of a degree-`d` fraction whose numerator is a local section of the
degree-`d` Rees piece: the one with the numerator transported to the local Rees algebra and back,
and the one with the numerator left alone.

Stated as a declaration rather than proved inline, because `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk` at
the sheaf-substrate grading is elaborated here against an expected type — inside a tactic proof
the same expression sends the `GradedRing` instance of that grading to synthesis, which fails on
the `abbrev` `…RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.grading`. -/
private theorem awayMk_reesChartGradedInv_hom
    (y : Γ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).piece (d : ℤ), (chartSite U).toOpens))
    (hw : reesChartGradedInv I (chartSite U) (reesChartGradedHom I (chartSite U)
          (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y)) ∈
        ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U) (d • 1)) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk
        (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
        (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a) d
        (reesChartGradedInv I (chartSite U) (reesChartGradedHom I (chartSite U)
          (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y)))
        hw =
      HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk
        (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
        (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a) d
        (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y)
        (of_mem_grading_smul_one (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I) (chartSite U).toOpens y) :=
  awayMk_congr _ _ _ _ _ (reesChartGradedInv_hom_apply I (chartSite U) _)

/-- **A degree-`d` fraction of the Rees algebra, read in the standard blowup chart.** The
fraction `x / aᵈ` of a local section `x` of the degree-`d` Rees piece over `U`, formed on the
degree-one `Proj` chart at `a`, is the affine blowup algebra's fraction of the image of `x` in
`Γ(X, U)`. -/
private theorem chartAwayEquiv_awayMk_of
    (y : Γ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).piece (d : ℤ), (chartSite U).toOpens)) :
    chartAwayEquiv I U a
        (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk
          ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).grading (chartSite U).toOpens)
          (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a) d
          (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y)
          (of_mem_grading_smul_one (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I) (chartSite U).toOpens y)) =
      _root_.affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
        (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d
        ⟨reesPieceAmbient I (d : ℤ) U.1 y,
          reesPieceAmbient_mem_affine I (d : ℤ) (Int.natCast_nonneg d) U y⟩ := by
  have hx : reesChartGradedHom I (chartSite U)
      (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y) ∈
      (AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation I).sectionRingGrading U.1 d :=
    Graded.map_mem _
      ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).of_mem_grading (chartSite U).toOpens y)
  have hx' : reesChartGradedHom I (chartSite U)
      (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y) ∈
      (AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation I).sectionRingGrading U.1 (d • 1) := by
    simpa using hx
  have h1 := HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map_mk (reesChartGradedInv I (chartSite U))
    (AlgebraicGeometry.reesDegreeOne I U a).1 (AlgebraicGeometry.reesDegreeOne I U a).2 d
    (reesChartGradedHom I (chartSite U)
      (DirectSum.of ((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).sectionPieces (chartSite U).toOpens) d y)) hx'
  have h2 := awayMk_reesChartGradedInv_hom I U a y
    (Graded.map_mem (reesChartGradedInv I (chartSite U)) hx')
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (chartAwayEquiv I U a) (h2.symm.trans h1.symm)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (chartAwayEquiv_awayMap I U a _) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (reesToAffineBlowupEquiv_awayMk I U a d _ hx) ?_
  exact congrArg (fun w : ↥(I.ideal U ^ d) =>
      _root_.affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
        (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d w)
    (Subtype.ext (reesToBase_reesChartGradedHom_of I U d y))

/-- The image in `Γ(X, U)` of a local section of `ℱ` under `ℱ ⟶ 𝒜_d ⟶ 𝒪_X` is the one
`Stacks.Blowup.reesPieceAmbient` gives to the underlying local section of the degree-`d` Rees
piece: the inclusion of a submodule of a sheaf of modules is `Subtype.val` on sections, so this
holds by `rfl`.

This is what makes the two generating families of `map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq_span` agree, the one
indexed by `↥(ℱ.toSubmodule.obj (op U))` and the one indexed by `Γ(ℱ.toSheafOfModules, U)`. -/
private theorem reesPieceAmbient_eq_structureAppₗ (s : ℱ.toSubmodule.obj (op U.1)) :
    reesPieceAmbient I (d : ℤ) U.1 s.1 = structureAppₗ (reesSubmoduleHom I ℱ) U.1 s := rfl

include pres in
/-- **The second centre, read on the standard blowup chart at `a`.** Its ideal in
`Γ(X, U)[I/a]` is generated by the fractions `x / aᵈ` for `x` a local section of `ℱ` over `U`:
this is the one statement that
`Stacks.Blowup.comap_reesCentre_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff` asks of the second centre. -/
private theorem map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq_span
    (hqc : ((ℱ.toSheafOfModules : X.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent)
    (hmem : ∀ x : Γ(ℱ.toSheafOfModules, U.1),
      structureAppₗ (reesSubmoduleHom I ℱ) U.1 x ∈ I.ideal U ^ d) :
    Ideal.map (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartΓIso I U a).hom.hom
        (Z.ideal (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartOpen I U a)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : Γ(ℱ.toSheafOfModules, U.1) =>
        _root_.affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
          (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d
          ⟨structureAppₗ (reesSubmoduleHom I ℱ) U.1 x, hmem x⟩) := by
  refine Eq.trans (map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq_map_chartAwayEquiv I U a Z) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun J : Ideal (HomogeneousLocalization.Away
        (((reesSheafGradedAlgebra I).toGradedAlgebra).grading (chartSite U))
        (reesSheafDegreeOne I U a)) =>
      Ideal.map (chartAwayEquiv I U a).toRingHom J)
    ((map_ΓSpecIso_ideal_comap_awayChart I ℱ Z pres U a).trans
      (ker_awayMap_sectionHom_eq_span_degreeOne (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I) ℱ pres.hom hqc
        pres.kernel (isAffineOpen_toOpens (chartSite U))
        (reesSheafDegreeOne_mem I U a)))) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Ideal.map_span (chartAwayEquiv I U a).toRingHom _) ?_
  exact congrArg Ideal.span ((Set.range_comp _ _).symm.trans
    (congrArg Set.range (funext fun s => (chartAwayEquiv_awayMk_of I U a s.1).trans
      (congrArg (fun w : ↥(I.ideal U ^ d) =>
          _root_.affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction (S := Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1)))
            (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) d w)
        (Subtype.ext (reesPieceAmbient_eq_structureAppₗ I ℱ U s))))))

end Chart

/-- **The existence of the second centre, [Stacks, Tag 080B].** -/
public theorem exists_secondCentre [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (hI : I.IsFiniteType)
    (Z : (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I).IdealSheafData) (hZft : Z.IsFiniteType) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ) (J : X.IdealSheafData), 0 < d ∧ J.IsFiniteType ∧ J ≤ I ^ d ∧
      J.comap (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase I) =
        AlgebraicGeometry.exceptionalIdeal I ^ d * Z := by
  have hWft : (Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom).IsFiniteType := hZft.comap _
  have hfp : AlgebraicGeometry.FinitePresentation
      (Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom).subschemeι := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.finitePresentation_iff_fg_ker,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι]
    exact hWft
  have : QuasiCompact (relativeProj (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I)).toBase :=
    quasiCompact_relativeProj_reesSheafGradedAlgebra_toBase I hI
  obtain ⟨d, hd, ℱ, hqc, hft, -, ⟨pres⟩⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.exists_finiteType_presentation_supp
      (reesSheafGradedAlgebra I) (Z.comap (reesProjBlowUpIso I).hom).subschemeι (⊥ : X.Opens)
      hfp (by simp) (by simp)
      (fun n => isFiniteType_reesSheafGradedAlgebra_piece I hI n)
  have := hqc
  have := hft
  refine ⟨d, reesCentre I ℱ, hd, isFiniteType_reesCentre I ℱ, reesCentre_le_pow I ℱ, ?_⟩
  rw [comap_reesCentre_eq_exceptionalIdeal_pow_mul_iff I ℱ Z]
  intro U a
  exact map_chartΓIso_ideal_eq_span I ℱ Z pres U a hqc
    (fun x => Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.ideal_le_ideal_pow I (reesCentre_le_pow I ℱ) U
      (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.structureAppₗ_mem_idealSheafDataOfHom
        (reesSubmoduleHom I ℱ) U x))

end Stacks.Blowup

end
